  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public-Private Partnership for the Dutch water sector in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment involves exploring opportunities for Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs) in the Dutch water sector&apos;s collaboration with Bangladesh, beyond Official Development Assistance (ODA).Following a workshop highlighting the sector&apos;s vision and strategy, the consultant&apos;s objectives include analysing the feasibility of a government-to-government Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) for PPPs, assessing ways to implement successful PPP projects under the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100, and drafting an action plan for the Dutch water sector&apos;s engagement in PPPs.The timeline spans from 1 January 2024 to 30 April 2024, with key deliverables including a report, a plan of action, and progress updates.</narrative>
  </description>
